.\" lwdbg(1) — mdoc, not man macros: it is the native format on the BSDs and
.\" GNU groff renders it without complaint.
.Dd November 3, 2026
.Dt LWDBG 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm lwdbg
.Nd measure, debug and control browsers through a caching proxy and a correlated debug store
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -home Ar dir
.Op Fl -json
.Ar command
.Op Ar arguments
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
measures and debugs web page loads.
It has two things no single-browser tool
has: a proxy every engine can be pointed at, and a store that correlates every
signal under one trace id.
.Pp
The proxy is the backbone because it is the only engine-agnostic layer.
It
reaches Gecko, Blink, WebKit and Goanna alike, including Pale Moon and
Basilisk where no extension can be installed at all.
Gecko browsers
additionally support Marionette, the DevTools remote protocol and WebDriver
BiDi, and an extension that can act on a session already running.
.Pp
Two rules are built into the tool because ignoring either produces confident
nonsense:
.Bl -enum -width 2n
.It
Measurements default to three runs and report the median with the spread.
A
single observation is not a property of a server; the origin this tool was
built against was measured swinging from 0.22 s to a 180 s timeout.
.It
A browser measurement is worth nothing without a non-browser baseline.
.Ic lwdbg measure --via curl
is the anchor.
If the two disagree by much more than 20% on TTFB, the browser
path is instrumented wrong and nothing downstream is trustworthy.
.El
.Sh GLOBAL OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width "--home dir"
.It Fl -home Ar dir
Store directory holding the SQLite database, the content-addressed blobs and
the local CA.
Defaults to
.Ev LWDBG_HOME ,
else
.Pa ~/.local/share/lwdbg .
.It Fl -json
Machine-readable output.
Use it whenever another program or agent consumes the
result.
.El
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width "adapters"
.It Ic doctor
What works on this machine and what is missing, with a remedy for each gap.
The first call in an unfamiliar environment.
.It Ic detect
Installed browsers, their engines, and which transports each can actually use.
Resolves symlinks, so a browser installed on another volume is reported at its
real location.
.It Ic proxy Cm start Ns | Ns Cm ca-export Ns | Ns Cm ca-install Ns | Ns Cm ca-uninstall
Run the intercepting cache, or manage its certificate authority.
.Fl -only-host
restricts interception to the named hosts and their subdomains; everything
else is tunnelled without being decrypted.
.It Ic measure Ar url
Three runs and a median.
.Fl -via
selects
.Cm curl ,
.Cm marionette ,
.Cm bidi
or
.Cm rdp ;
anything but
.Cm curl
needs
.Fl -browser .
.It Ic launch
Start a browser with debug transports enabled, in a scratch profile this tool
created.
It refuses any profile directory it did not create.
.It Ic attach
Connect to a transport that is already listening and report what is there.
.It Ic eval Ar script
Run JavaScript in a browser reached over a transport.
Pairs with
.Ic launch
to drive a session by hand.
.It Ic live
Act on a browser that is already running, through the extension bridge.
Commands that change state are refused unless
.Fl -allow-write
is given.
.It Ic parity
Compare how browsers render the same URL, on the GPU where one is available
and on the CPU always.
The CPU path is the reference implementation.
.It Ic android
Android Firefox over
.Xr adb 1 :
socket discovery, port forwarding, real multitouch input and screen capture.
.It Ic vantage Ar url
Measure the same target from other machines over ssh.
Two or more vantage
points are what separates a slow origin from a slow route.
.It Ic logs Cm modules Ns | Ns Cm ingest
What
.Ev MOZ_LOG
can collect, and how to fold a log file into the store.
.It Ic ssot Cm traces Ns | Ns Cm trace Ns | Ns Cm compression
Query the store.
.Cm compression
answers whether compression actually applied, from recorded wire and decoded
byte counts rather than from a header.
.It Ic adapters Cm list Ns | Ns Cm install Ns | Ns Cm emit Ns | Ns Cm uninstall
Wire this tool into the agent harnesses on this machine from one canonical
source.
A path that was inferred rather than observed is reported as such.
.El
.Pp
.Ic lwdbg Ar command Fl h
is the authoritative syntax for each.
This page is the map, not the manual.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width LWDBG_SKILL
.It Ev LWDBG_HOME
Store directory.
Overridden by
.Fl -home .
.It Ev LWDBG_SKILL
Directory holding
.Pa SKILL.md
and
.Pa references/ .
Searched first; then the directory baked in at build time by
.Ic make install ;
then paths relative to the executable; then the current directory.
.It Ev LWDBG_LOG
Tracing filter, in
.Xr env_logger 3
syntax, e.g.
.Li lwdbg_proxy=debug .
Diagnostics go to standard error.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "~/.local/share/lwdbg/store/live.sock" -compact
.It Pa ~/.local/share/lwdbg/store/
SQLite database and content-addressed blobs.
.It Pa ~/.local/share/lwdbg/ca/
Local certificate authority.
The private key is mode 0600.
.It Pa ~/.local/share/lwdbg/store/live.sock
Socket the extension bridge listens on, mode 0600.
.It Pa PREFIX/share/lwdbg/skills/librewolf-debugger/
Installed skill and reference tree.
.It Pa PREFIX/share/lwdbg/extension/
The WebExtension, to load through
.Pa about:debugging .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Ic doctor
exits non-zero when a required tool is missing, having printed every check
first rather than stopping at the first failure.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr adb 1 ,
.Xr certutil 1 ,
.Xr curl 1 ,
.Xr ssh 1
.Pp
.Pa PREFIX/share/lwdbg/skills/librewolf-debugger/references/
holds the long-form notes: engine and transport matrices, the LibreWolf
specifics, proxy and CA mechanics, logging, parity, Android, vantage hosts,
building and packaging.
.Sh CAVEATS
On LibreWolf the DevTools remote protocol cannot be enabled at all.
Its
.Pa librewolf.cfg
forces
.Li devtools.debugger.remote-enabled
false with a plain
.Fn pref
call, and AutoConfig is applied after
.Pa user.js ,
so no user preference can override it.
.Fl -start-debugger-server
is then accepted and silently does nothing.
Marionette and WebDriver BiDi
both work; consequently a LibreWolf instance that is already running is
reachable only through the extension bridge or the proxy.
.Sh SECURITY CONSIDERATIONS
.Bl -bullet
.It
A proxy with a trusted CA sees
.Em all
traffic from any browser pointed at it, credentials and session cookies
included.
Scope every capture with
.Fl -only-host ,
and do not leave a capture-all proxy running after the task.
.It
Tor Browser is refused unless
.Fl -force-tor
is given.
A local interception breaks its threat model.
.It
.Ic live
acts on the user's real session, with their logins in it.
The host refuses a
state-changing command without
.Fl -allow-write ,
and the refusal happens before anything reaches the browser.
That is a
mechanism, not a substitute for asking: approval for one action is not
approval for the next.
.It
.Ic launch
writes
.Li devtools.debugger.prompt-connection=false
and
.Li privacy.resistFingerprinting=false
into its profile.
Both would remove protections from a profile somebody
browses with, so it refuses any directory it did not create.
.It
Remove the CA when the work is done:
.Ic lwdbg proxy ca-uninstall --profile Ar dir .
.El
